/*  FUNCTION NAME:      NTHOCCURRENCE
    DESCRIPTION:*//**Returns a running count of each value's occurrences in a 1D array.*/
/*  RETURNS:            array: running count of each value's occurrences so far, same shape as the input
    PARAMETERS:
        arr             (Required) A 1D array (row or column) of values (text, numbers, or mixed).
    EXAMPLE:            =NTHOCCURRENCE({"A";"S";"S";"A";"M";"A"}) -> {1;1;2;2;1;3}
    REVISIONS:          Date        Developer   Description
                        2026-04-14  Claude      Initial version
                        2026-11-09  Claude      Count with XMATCH keys and SORTBY instead of a MAP of SUMPRODUCTs: 5-9x faster at 500-5000 rows. An error in the input now gives an error in its own row only; it used to turn every later row into an error (#56)
                        2026-11-09  Claude      Help table removed from the formula; its text is the header metadata the argument hints read (#381, #382)
*/
NTHOCCURRENCE = LAMBDA(
//  Parameter Declarations
    [arr],
    LET(
    //  Procedure
        raw, TOCOL(arr),
    //  Numbers to 15 significant digits, as = compares them (0.1+0.2 = 0.3); XMATCH alone wouldn't
        col, IF(ISNUMBER(raw), IFERROR(--(raw & ""), raw), raw),
        n, ROWS(col),
        idx, SEQUENCE(n),
    //  Each value's key is the position of its first occurrence. Sorting the positions by
    //  (key, position) puts each value's occurrences together in order; a row's count is its
    //  place in that sorted list less the place where its group starts, sorted back.
        key, XMATCH(col, col),
        order, SORTBY(idx, key, 1, idx, 1),
        sortedKey, INDEX(key, order),
        running, SORTBY(idx - XMATCH(sortedKey, sortedKey) + 1, order, 1),
        result, IF(COLUMNS(arr) > 1, TRANSPOSE(running), running),
        result
)
);
